{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_42f8b51d9c4943029c62e10d087e8171","id":"pg_1d40d41ab8085707869c2983fc5ae084","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openbmb-chatdev-docs-user-guide-zh-modules-memory-md-4fb2db0ea903-2983fc5ae084.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_2b6d7e37073056b48846df2a4c673243"],"title":"OpenBMB/ChatDev/docs/user_guide/zh/modules/memory.md @ 4fb2db0ea903","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42f8b51d9c4943029c62e10d087e8171"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_4b0c04c68b0b3663363980086499526722e0b608797c34729b7dcd0b62314c27"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent nodes attach memories via MemoryAttachmentConfig with fields for store name, retrieve_stage, top_k (default 3), similarity_threshold, and read/write flags; retrieved items are injected into the agent context and writes occur after node completion."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d7537b2c88ec5bfdb16c8b73c39c243c7eb6238b84151fa60e4b0e0b31c1a060"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The memory system offers four built-in store types: simple (FAISS plus semantic rerank, read/write), file (read-only vector index over documents), blackboard (append-only recency log), and mem0 (cloud-managed, requires the mem0ai package)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_4b0c04c68b0b3663363980086499526722e0b608797c34729b7dcd0b62314c27","clm_d7537b2c88ec5bfdb16c8b73c39c243c7eb6238b84151fa60e4b0e0b31c1a060"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_42f8b51d9c4943029c62e10d087e8171","id":"pg_271fe2ae1d52576da37052639e896339","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openbmb-chatdev-docs-user-guide-en-modules-memory-md-4fb2db0ea903-52639e896339.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_daa8306a64875810a02f47980fdc9366"],"title":"OpenBMB/ChatDev/docs/user_guide/en/modules/memory.md @ 4fb2db0ea903","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42f8b51d9c4943029c62e10d087e8171"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_42f8b51d9c4943029c62e10d087e8171","id":"pg_3f4da125226b5c7e91a78c42108026fd","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openbmb-chatdev-requirements-txt-4fb2db0ea903-8c42108026fd.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_2730bf6191635a81b31156ef15c88e66"],"title":"OpenBMB/ChatDev/requirements.txt @ 4fb2db0ea903","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42f8b51d9c4943029c62e10d087e8171"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_267909084b2727ecf4b3a5f6b655ea8f8055cb5846f1bbd5803217272c34fbf3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Python SDK exposes run_workflow (from runtime.sdk) taking a YAML file, task prompt, attachments, and variable overrides, returning a result with a final message; it is also published on PyPI as chatdev 0.1.0."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2ffa16cbf093b932782b37191564262314acb9ccd74b5c51171327494dd7d1ba"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is modular: server/ hosts the FastAPI backend, runtime/ handles agent abstraction and tool execution, workflow/ contains multi-agent logic driven by entity/ configs, frontend/ is a Vue 3 web console, and functions/ holds custom Python tools."},{"claim_ids":["clm_563418ec0285f29a25a49e207e04deb499f4416b56c9d1a38e968891fe508b39"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prerequisites are macOS/Linux/WSL/Windows, Python 3.12+, Node.js 18+, and the uv package manager; Python dependencies are synced with uv sync and frontend dependencies with npm install."},{"claim_ids":["clm_65d83930604d5d2125e877ac5333874b17ed6a6c1171b977ac64ac067dae2941"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Out-of-the-box YAML workflow templates ship in yaml_instance/, covering data visualization, Blender-based 3D generation, game development, deep research, and teaching-video scenarios."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7743aebec48fc5047881a063b8487fe6e227b507c1366ec778bfa6e9c13272a2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The application can be started with make dev, or manually via uv run python server_main.py --port 6400 for the backend and a frontend dev server on port 5173 with VITE_API_BASE_URL pointing at the backend."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a699ba226554947ccf84644cbaf2b34b2b7d08329a9439ff670f6cd86989670f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The web console includes a visual drag-and-drop workflow canvas for configuring node parameters and context flows, plus a Launch tab to run workflows, watch real-time logs, inspect artifacts, and give human-in-the-loop feedback."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b436a660288c396288fbd47e94f772cdd08e2eb1d3104f4684ac14685c15d8f7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ChatDev 1.0, the legacy 'Virtual Software Company' with CEO/CTO/Programmer-style agents automating the software lifecycle, has been moved to the chatdev1.0 branch for maintenance."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d4261314489e9628f0af62079f341f006bc760f9e1c3aad9245c98fb517d401c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ChatDev 2.0 (DevAll) is described as a zero-code multi-agent platform where users define agents, workflows, and tasks via configuration for scenarios such as data visualization, 3D generation, and deep research."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f1d65bd27a4a9c5932319a3e835f4db76905fef863fc658bb5f45857d7295953"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Alternatively the whole application runs via Docker Compose (docker compose up --build) with backend on port 6400 and frontend on 5173; services auto-restart on crash and local file changes are reflected in containers."}],"claim_ids":["clm_267909084b2727ecf4b3a5f6b655ea8f8055cb5846f1bbd5803217272c34fbf3","clm_2ffa16cbf093b932782b37191564262314acb9ccd74b5c51171327494dd7d1ba","clm_563418ec0285f29a25a49e207e04deb499f4416b56c9d1a38e968891fe508b39","clm_65d83930604d5d2125e877ac5333874b17ed6a6c1171b977ac64ac067dae2941","clm_7743aebec48fc5047881a063b8487fe6e227b507c1366ec778bfa6e9c13272a2","clm_a699ba226554947ccf84644cbaf2b34b2b7d08329a9439ff670f6cd86989670f","clm_b436a660288c396288fbd47e94f772cdd08e2eb1d3104f4684ac14685c15d8f7","clm_d4261314489e9628f0af62079f341f006bc760f9e1c3aad9245c98fb517d401c","clm_f1d65bd27a4a9c5932319a3e835f4db76905fef863fc658bb5f45857d7295953"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_42f8b51d9c4943029c62e10d087e8171","id":"pg_4f4a92409eec5ae1860312a24880a371","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openbmb-chatdev-readme-md-4fb2db0ea903-12a24880a371.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0"